2026-05-14  Ivan S. Titov  <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com>

	2.0.0_rc2 — "First CI Run + Packaging Polish"

	Three CI cycles on gentoo/stage3:latest after rc1 surfaced 5
	shellcheck --severity=error violations (rc1 dev host didn't have
	shellcheck installed locally; make distcheck passed but the CI
	`shellcheck --severity=error src/portconf` step failed before any
	test tier ran).  Fixes for all five are below, plus the routine
	work of preparing the audited tree for release: Gentoo ebuilds,
	editor/shellcheck config baselines, a CI-locked dist sanity-check,
	GitHub issue templates and contribution guide, AI-assistance
	disclosure.  281 bats tests pass (178 unit + 70 integration +
	32 smoke + 1 root-conditional) against a shellcheck-clean source.

	Source-side fixes:
	* src/portconf.in (sort_uses, sort_keywords): SC2066 — the
	  `for option in "$(...)"` loop pattern (double-quoted command
	  substitution) iterates exactly once.  Replaced with a direct
	  `atom_opts+="$(...)"` append; same semantics, less code.
	* src/portconf.in (mask_trash slot_output / non_slot_output):
	  SC2104 — `continue 2` inside an inner function works in bash
	  (the directive propagates up through the function call to the
	  enclosing loop) but is non-portable.  Refactored: the helpers
	  set `_trash_hit=1`; the inner unmask loop adds
	      (( _trash_hit )) && break
	  at the end of its body.  Same control-flow effect — break inner
	  → outer continues naturally — without the function-level loop
	  magic.  Per-outer-iteration `_trash_hit=0` reset added.
	* src/portconf.in (dispatcher tail): SC2199 — `[[ -z "${@}" ]]`
	  works only because `${@}` implicitly concatenates inside [[ ]].
	  Replaced with `[[ $# -eq 0 ]]`.
	* src/portconf.in: SC2199-fix comment rephrasing — shellcheck
	  parsed `# shellcheck SC2199: ...` as a directive (the canonical
	  form is `disable=SCxxxx`) and bailed with SC1072/SC1073 on the
	  second CI run.  Comment now starts with prose; the SC2199
	  reference is preserved in the body.

	Cosmetic shellcheck pass:
	* src/portconf.in: 18 warning-level findings down to 3.  Dead
	  variables removed (newest in backup / world_backup;
	  installed_vers / installed_min_ver / installed_max_ver /
	  installed_live_ver in check_uses).  ${*} for the opts assembly
	  (was implicit ${@}-as-string).  Quoted `$(_cols)` in the three
	  fold-pipeline sites.  `# shellcheck disable=` and
	  `# shellcheck source=/dev/null` directives at the four runtime-
	  resolved source-call sites and the variadic _mktemp forwarder
	  and the intentional column-placeholder `read` in mask_trash.
	  No behaviour change — diff is comments + idiomatic spellings +
	  7 lines of dead code removed.
	* The remaining 3 warnings are SC2010 (`ls | grep`) patterns in
	  repo_fix / f_to_d / d_to_f.  Functional rewrites; explicitly
	  deferred to 2.1.0.

	Tests:
	* tests/unit/diff_ask.bats: root-conditional Yes-branch coverage.
	  The existing "interactive Yes as non-root — exits 1" test
	  passes only as a non-root UID; CI on gentoo/stage3:latest runs
	  as root and would hit the mv+chmod branch instead.  Gated with
	  `(( UID == 0 )) && skip`, plus a complementary root-branch
	  test gated with `(( UID != 0 )) && skip`.  Together they cover
	  both branches in their respective environments.

	Packaging:
	* packaging/portconf.ebuild.in: EAPI=8 release ebuild for the
	  ::stuff overlay.  RDEPEND covers bash 4.4+, eix, portage-utils,
	  tre, portage; bash-completion is optional.  src_test runs the
	  unit suite, probes the eix cache, and conditionally runs the
	  integration suite when the cache is populated.  pkg_postinst
	  reminds about eix-update.
	* packaging/portconf-9999.ebuild: live ebuild inheriting git-r3,
	  no KEYWORDS, with autoconf/automake added to BDEPEND and
	  eautoreconf in src_prepare.
	* packaging/metadata.xml: maintainer, longdesc, USE flag docs,
	  GitHub remote-id.
	* packaging/Makefile.am: `make ebuild OVERLAY_DIR=...` recipe
	  drops a versioned ebuild + metadata.xml into the given overlay
	  and runs `ebuild ... manifest` to fetch the dist tarball and
	  write Manifest.  Top-level Makefile.am delegates.

	Build:
	* .editorconfig: whitespace rules for shells, bats, ebuilds,
	  autoconf, YAML, ChangeLog.  Shipped in EXTRA_DIST.
	* .shellcheckrc: encodes the SC2010 deferrals (3 sites in
	  repo_fix / f_to_d / d_to_f) so local shellcheck matches CI
	  behaviour.
	* Makefile.am: new installcheck-local target — verifies installed
	  $(bindir)/portconf reports the expected version and that
	  --help works.  Honors DESTDIR for staging installs.
	* configure.ac: bump to 2.0.0_rc2.

	CI:
	* .github/workflows/ci.yml: dist sanity-check switched from
	  `make dist` to `make distcheck`.  `make dist` only produces the
	  tarball; `make distcheck` extracts it into an isolated subdir
	  and runs configure + make + make check + make install + make
	  uninstall against it — catches missing EXTRA_DIST entries,
	  srcdir-vs-builddir bugs, and install-target breakage that plain
	  `make dist` would not surface.

	Docs:
	* README.md: CI status badge, markdown links for ChangeLog +
	  INSTALL, ::stuff overlay add-overlay URL.
	* AUTHORS, README.md, ChangeLog: AI usage disclosure block —
	  Claude (Anthropic) used as a coding assistant; every change
	  reviewed by hand and validated against bats unit + integration
	  + smoke + shellcheck + make distcheck before landing.
	* CONTRIBUTING.md: contribution guide covering bug reports,
	  feature proposals, PR workflow (with the new-flag checklist),
	  commit messages, code style, signing, license.
	* .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/{bug_report,feature_request,config}.yml:
	  GitHub issue forms — version + environment + command output +
	  expected/actual + relevant /etc/portage file content (with
	  flag-to-file pairing table); minimal feature template.
	* ChangeLog: corrected stale commit-hash references and the
	  broken rebrand from-to in the rc1 and pre5 entries; added the
	  missing smoke-helper entries (help.bats, profile.bats) to pre5;
	  updated test-count, bug-count, and `|| true` figures to match
	  current state.

	Note: the rc1 tag and the rc1 ChangeLog entry below are preserved
	verbatim — rc1 was a real (failed-CI) state.  rc2 is the same
	source tree plus the post-rc1 fixes, the cosmetic shellcheck
	pass, packaging, configs, CI hardening, and contribution docs.

	* AI-assisted: the 2.0.0_rc2 work used Claude (Anthropic) as a
	  coding assistant.  Every change was reviewed by hand and
	  validated against the bats unit, integration, and smoke layers,
	  shellcheck, and `make distcheck` before landing.

2026-05-14  Ivan S. Titov  <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com>

	2.0.0_rc1 — "Audited Pretty Far Down"

	Post-pre5 hardening round.  Critical code review of the pre5 tree
	surfaced 3 HIGH-severity correctness items and 4 MEDIUM-severity
	hardening opportunities, all addressed.  Plus the 0.1.0 → 2.0.0
	version-namespace rebrand acknowledging that the modernisation is a
	major-version successor to megabaks's 1.6.x line, not a fresh 0.x
	project.

	Branch state: 280 bats tests in three tiers (178 unit + 70 integration
	+ 32 smoke).  Fourteen cumulative latent-bug fixes across all rounds.

	HIGH-severity fixes:
	* src/portconf.in (package_env): sed `s|${line}|${new_line}|` was
	  interpolating raw user content from package.env.  Atoms with
	  USE-dep brackets like `sys-apps/grep[static]`, pipes in comments,
	  or dots in conf names corrupted the in-place edit.  Fixed via the
	  same escape pattern used in invalid_uses_make's _p/_r block,
	  extended to also escape `[` and `*`.
	* src/portconf.in (mask_trash): hoisted the `eix -e "${cat}/${pn}"`
	  call out of the inner unmask loop — it depends only on outer-loop
	  variables.  Previous nested shape was O(N×M) eix forks (up to
	  2500 for a typical 50+50 mask/unmask config); now O(N) with a
	  lazy-fetch fallback for the rare case where mver is empty but
	  the first inner iteration has a non-empty uver.
	* src/portconf.in (regen_world): `qlist -CI $(emerge -epO system |
	  awk '/\[/ {print $4}')` with empty awk output ran `qlist -CI`
	  with zero atom args and returned the FULL installed list — every
	  installed atom then landed in `pretend`, every atom matched the
	  filter, and the @world cleanup was a no-op.  Fixed by capturing
	  the system-atoms list and skipping the qlist append entirely
	  when empty.

	Cascade fix:
	* src/portconf.in (file_or_dir callers): with the pre5 file_or_dir
	  fix (ls set-e abort + dead-`[[ -z "${founded}" ]]` check) now
	  firing the diagnostic properly for the first time, 11 callers
	  that wrote `file_or_dir ... || return 1` started actually
	  propagating the "missing target" signal — which then aborted
	  dispatch arms like -t mid-chain.  All these callers are
	  processing OPTIONAL config files; changed to `|| true` at all
	  11 sites (rm_comments, rm_all_comments, sort_use_file,
	  sort_keywords, uniq_keywords, package_env_conf, package_env,
	  all_mask_trash×2, stupid_unmask, check_use_masked).  No behavioural change
	  vs. the historical (broken) silent-no-op state; the diagnostic
	  message is now visible without breaking composite dispatch.

	MEDIUM-severity hardening:
	* src/portconf.in (color codes): emitted only when `[ -t 1 ]` AND
	  `${NO_COLOR:-}` is unset (https://no-color.org).  Pipe/redirect
	  contexts now get clean machine-readable output.
	* src/portconf.in (tput): all 17 raw `tput` call sites now go
	  through `_tput`/`_cols` wrappers that no-op when stdout isn't a
	  TTY.  `_cols` falls back to 80 columns.  Fixes hang/error
	  behaviour in pipes and unset-$TERM contexts.
	* src/portconf.in (sed-injection at 3 milder sites): new helpers
	  `_sed_escape_pat` and `_sed_escape_rep` applied at sort_uses,
	  sort_keywords, and not_found.  Atoms with USE-dep brackets,
	  dots in versions, or wildcards no longer slip past the regex
	  match.
	* src/portconf.in (set -f containment): `local -` (bash 4.4+)
	  added at function entry of invalid_uses, invalid_uses_make,
	  not_found, and f_to_d to guarantee globbing-state
	  restoration on any return path — including set -e aborts mid-
	  function.  Redundant trailing `set +f` calls removed where the
	  scope was function-level.
	* src/portconf.in: walked all 105 `|| true` patches; no findings.
	  Every one defensive against expected empty-result tool output
	  (grep on no-match, awk on empty input, find on missing dir).

	Rebrand:
	* configure.ac, man/portconf.1, ChangeLog: 0.1.0 → 2.0.0 across
	  every tracked version reference.  The 0.1.0_pre1..pre4 tags
	  were renamed to 2.0.0_pre1..pre4 in the same commit — same
	  commit objects, new tag names.  Pre-rebrand commit-message
	  strings still say "0.1.0_pre*" as a historical record.

	New tests:
	* tests/integration/package_env.bats (6 tests, new file) — regression
	  for HIGH#1 sed-injection.  Covers atoms with [USE] brackets,
	  pipes in comments, dots in conf names, plus happy-path
	  present/missing-conf cases.
	* tests/integration/regen_world.bats (+1 test) — explicit regression
	  for HIGH#3.  Sets EMERGE_SYSTEM="" and verifies @world still
	  gets cleaned (vs. pre-fix where it stayed empty).  Existing 6
	  tests dropped their `EMERGE_SYSTEM='sentinel/atom'` workaround.
	* tests/smoke/no_color.bats (4 tests, new file) — regression for
	  MEDIUM#4.  Asserts --version, --help, -apu produce no ANSI
	  escapes when stdout is non-TTY; plus explicit NO_COLOR=1 check.

	Build:
	* configure.ac: bump to 2.0.0_rc1.

	Docs:
	* COPYING: full FSF GPL-3.0 text added (verbatim, byte-identical
	  to Gentoo's /var/db/repos/gentoo/licenses/GPL-3).  Megabaks's
	  upstream and every 1.5.x/1.6.x tag asserted the license only in
	  the script header line; no COPYING/LICENSE was ever shipped.
	  Adding it does NOT change terms — just makes the long-standing
	  assertion machine-discoverable (GitHub License sidebar, Gentoo
	  ebuild LICENSE matching, SPDX scanners) and ships the canonical
	  text with the source tarball.  Makefile.am EXTRA_DIST updated.
	* README.md: refreshed for the 2.0.0 candidate — maintained-fork note,
	  280-test suite mention, env-overridable path roots section
	  (for chroot / sandbox users), explicit COPYING reference.
	  Dropped the "Install from ::stuff overlay ONLY" line since
	  INSTALL now documents from-source installation alongside the
	  overlay path.
	* AUTHORS, README.md: scrubbed two references to "bash-revival",
	  which was a local-workspace-directory label only, never a
	  published project name or organisation.

	Note on the rc1 vs pre5 naming: pre5 was a "feature work in
	progress" snapshot; rc1 represents the candidate state for 2.0.0
	final.  Outstanding LOW-severity items from the review (monolithic
	structure, leaf-function exit-1 usage, nested-function closures,
	help/dispatcher drift detection) are explicitly deferred to a
	2.1.0 cycle — they are architecture/maintainability concerns, not
	correctness blockers.

2026-05-14  Ivan S. Titov  <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com>

	2.0.0_pre5 — "Tested All The Way Down"

	First substantial pre-release.  Comprehensive modernisation of the
	inherited script across pre2 (style + safety), pre3-pre4
	(correctness — 12 bugs in three audit rounds), and pre5 (initial
	bats test suite).  Then the coverage round and bug-hunt that built
	out two more test tiers and surfaced 11 further latent bugs that
	had been silently mis-behaving on every modern Gentoo install of
	portconf, unnoticed because no test exercised the affected path.
	269 bats tests in three tiers (178 unit + 63 integration + 28
	smoke) at the end.

	Style and safety (pre2):
	* src/portconf.in: Replace all backtick command substitutions with
	  $().  Replace echo -e with printf '%b\n' throughout.  Full
	  quoting audit — fix all unquoted variable expansions.
	* src/portconf.in: set -euo pipefail enforced from line 4;
	  || true guards added to grep/diff used in command substitutions.
	  set -u + explicit initialisation of all accumulator variables.
	  Trap-based temp-file cleanup (_tmpfiles array / _cleanup).
	* src/portconf.in (overlays): Remove stray `unset PORTDIR_OVERLAY`
	  after local declaration.  Replace all for-in-$(find/ls) loops
	  with while IFS= read -r + process substitution.  Replace layman
	  with repos.conf parsing.  Eliminate IFS-manipulation workaround
	  loops.

	Correctness (pre3–pre4):
	* src/portconf.in: 12 bugs corrected — profile parent-traversal,
	  use_mask path quoting, IFS= on every read call, and
	  variable-quoting issues in sed/grep patterns.

	Source-side overridability:
	* src/portconf.in: Six system path roots now honor environment
	  overrides — PKGDB, BRDIR, PORT_ETC, WORLD, DEP_PATH, PORTCONF_CONF.
	  Defaults unchanged (canonical modern Gentoo layout); production
	  behaviour identical.
	* src/portconf.in (backup): tar working-dir derived from
	  ${PORT_ETC%/*}/ instead of hardcoded /etc/.  Legacy /etc/make.conf
	  inclusion gated on PORT_ETC == /etc/portage.
	* src/portconf.in (etc_restore): tar extract destination derived
	  from ${PORT_ETC%/*}/ instead of literal "/etc/".
	* src/portconf.in (overlays): reads ${PORT_ETC}/repos.conf (file +
	  directory glob) instead of /etc/portage/repos.conf.
	* src/portconf.in (current_profile, use_mask, pre_profile init):
	  honor ${PORT_ETC}/make.profile.

	Bug fixes (latent — surfaced by the test coverage round):
	* package_envs: rewritten for portage-utils 0.97+ qatom output
	  (operator now a trailing field; "<unset>" placeholder for missing
	  PV).  mask_trash had been broken on every Gentoo system since the
	  qatom format change.
	* overlays: `stop` accessed under set -u before fix_deps() set it
	  → unbound-variable crash on first dep-cache loop iteration.
	* overlays/fix_deps: /var/cache/edb/dep hardcoded — would rm -rf
	  real host cache when run with a stricter repos.conf.  Hoisted to
	  overridable global DEP_PATH at init.
	* overlays: `IFS= read -r path name` silently swallowed every
	  overlay entry — empty IFS disables field splitting.  `portconf
	  -fr` had never reported an unused overlay since this loop was
	  introduced.
	* restore(): `rm -rf "${5}"` with ${5}="${PORT_ETC}/*" never wiped
	  anything — bash doesn't glob inside double quotes.  etc_restore's
	  wipe-then-extract semantics had been a no-op.  Fix uses
	  `find ${dir} -mindepth 1 -delete`.
	* restore(): ${5} accessed under set -u when world_restore called
	  with only 4 args → unbound-variable crash.
	* regen_world: pretend-list concatenation lost the separator
	  newline → downstream ^atom$ lookups missed.
	* dispatcher (-ui, -uf, -t, -ft, -f): eix-cache cleanup compound
	  returned 1 under set -e when eix_cache was empty, propagating
	  to the script's exit.  Every mutating-flag run that reused the
	  existing eix cache silently exited 1.
	* package_env_conf: `find "${PORT_ETC}/env/"` aborted under set -e
	  when env/ didn't exist (the common case).
	* file_or_dir: `ls` failure aborted set -e before the "No such file"
	  diagnostic could fire; with that masked, `[[ -z "${founded}" ]]`
	  never matched because ${founded} always has a leading space.

	Tests (initial unit suite, pre5 batch):
	* tests/test_helper.bash: Saves and restores bats' EXIT trap
	  around the portconf.in source call (portconf sets `trap _cleanup
	  EXIT` at load time, silently overwriting bats' own teardown trap
	  under set -e).
	* tests/unit/test_helper.bash: Stubs eend/ebegin to prevent the
	  _update_tty_level 0<&1 FD-corruption crash inside bats subprocesses.
	* tests/unit/ (16 files, 136 tests): Unit suite covering
	  diff_ask, f_to_d/d_to_f, sort_uses/sort_use_file, empty_files/
	  backup_files, sort_uniq_files, uniq_keywords, sort_keywords,
	  sort_uniq_mask_use, ver_diff/ver_btwn, timestamp, backup,
	  repo_fix/rm_repo_fix, use_makeconf.
	* src/portconf.in (repo_fix): Add `|| true` inside the
	  local_categories command substitution to prevent a pipefail abort
	  when an overlay has no virtual/ directory.
	* src/portconf.in (not_found): Add `|| true` to the
	  `grep -v "${INVALID_FOUNDED}"` pipeline — grep exits 1 on empty
	  emerge output under set -o pipefail, killing not_found whenever
	  the INVALID path had already collected atoms.
	* tests/integration/ (3 files, 15 tests): Integration suite for
	  the three functions requiring live Portage tools.  eix and emerge
	  are stubbed in not_found tests (eix -Ttc reads real /etc/portage,
	  not PORT_ETC); real eix/qatom used for invalid_uses and
	  invalid_uses_make; agrep stubbed in invalid_uses.  Run separately
	  with `bats tests/integration/` or `make check-integration`.
	  Requires app-portage/eix, app-portage/portage-utils, dev-libs/tre.

	Tests (coverage-round additions, 151→269 across rounds):
	* tests/unit/check_use_masked.bats (10 tests) — twice-masked /
	  twice-unmasked / stupid-unmask / per-host-mask matrix.
	* tests/unit/world_backup.bats (8 tests) — tarball creation,
	  idempotency, rotation when count >= COUNT.
	* tests/unit/portconf_conf.bats (14 tests) — COUNT defaulting,
	  IGNORE_CATEGORY/IGNORE_PN regex expansion, PORTCONF_CONF override.
	* tests/unit/error_paths.bats (5 tests, new) — eix not installed,
	  file_or_dir missing target, backup auto-creates BRDIR.
	* tests/unit/diff_ask.bats (+5) — interactive Yes/No/bogus reprompt
	  branches; non-root Yes-exit-1 gating.
	* tests/integration/mask_trash.bats (16 tests) — unversioned +
	  versioned + slot-qualified atom branches.
	* tests/integration/stupid_unmask.bats (9 tests) — stupid entry
	  detection with installed/!installed labelling.
	* tests/integration/overlays.bats (6 tests) — UNUSED detection with
	  sandboxed PORT_ETC/PKGDB/DEP_PATH.
	* tests/integration/backup_path.bats (5 tests) — PORT_ETC + BRDIR
	  override contract.
	* tests/integration/restore.bats (5 tests) — etc_restore +
	  world_restore via bats <<< feeding bash's `select`.
	* tests/integration/regen_world.bats (6 tests) — stubbed emerge +
	  qlist; *-libs/, virtual/, and in-pretend exclusion filters.
	* tests/smoke/help.bats (9 tests, new file) — --help, -h, -?,
	  no-args, and unknown-flag dispatch paths exercised against the
	  built binary.
	* tests/smoke/profile.bats (4 tests, new file) — profile resolution
	  via eselect / eix sanity-checked end-to-end.
	* tests/smoke/mutating_flags.bats (15 tests, new) — every mutating
	  dispatch arm through the BUILT binary with sandboxed paths and
	  --pretend.  Covers -b, -c, -ac, -f2d, -wb, -s, -us, -ku, -ko,
	  -sm, -ui, -um, -t, -uf, -f.

	CI:
	* .github/workflows/ci.yml: smoke suite step added after the
	  integration tier.

	Docs:
	* INSTALL: "Environment overrides" section for the six overridable
	  path roots.

	Build:
	* configure.ac: bump to 2.0.0_pre5.

2026-05-12  Ivan S. Titov  <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com>

	Revival: 2.0.0 — "Back From 2014"

	First versioned release of the maintained fork. The original script
	by megabaks (https://github.com/megabaks/portconf) was last updated
	in March 2014; this release picks it up as-is and adds the
	infrastructure needed for ongoing maintenance.

	* configure.ac, Makefile.am, src/Makefile.am, man/Makefile.am:
	  New autotools build system.  `./configure && make && make install`
	  installs portconf to $(bindir) and portconf.conf to $(sysconfdir).
	* src/portconf.in: Script moved here; PACKAGE_VERSION substituted at
	  build time.  Added --version / -V flag.
	* man/portconf.1: New man page covering all flags, configuration, and
	  dependencies.
	* AUTHORS: megabaks as original author; istitov as maintainer.
	* INSTALL: Gentoo-specific installation notes.

	* AI-assisted: the build system, man page, and metadata files in
	  this release were authored with Claude (Anthropic) as a coding
	  assistant.  The portconf script itself is unchanged from
	  megabaks's original.  Every generated change was reviewed by
	  hand before landing.
